/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  BCM_APERTA2_DIRECT
 * REGISTER:  LMI_DEBUG_LMI_DEBUG
 * BLOCKS:   LMI_DEBUG
 * REGADDR:  0x9016
 * DESC:     LMI_DEBUG
 * RESETVAL: 0x0 (0)
 * ACCESS:   R/W
 * FIELDS:
 *     MDIO_DEBUG       This register is used when MDIO has to access registers for debug purposeFor Aperta2, LMI offers a debug mode where in MDIO can access registers via LMI for debug purposes, irrespective of the M0 status.There are 2 scenarios in which MDIO may need to access regsiters via LMI.1) When M0 is not responding2) When M0 is running and MDIO has to access registers for debug purposeThis register is only accessible by MDIO.Below are the steps for MDIO to gain accessStep1: Pause M0Step2: Unlock the debug bit by writing the code 16'hFAAB to the register, which instructs LMI that, from now on take instructions from MDIO.Step3: Reset LMIStep4: Read the desired registers via LMIStep5: Lock the debug bit by MDIO writing code 16'h0000 to instruct LMI that it can serve M0.Step6: Resume M0Please note that the above steps has to be followed by upper layer software. H/w will be switching the master based on the value of the lmi_debug register
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
